      "slug": "doubanjiang",
      "term": "Doubanjiang",
      "definition": "Sichuanese fermented broad bean and chilli paste. The defining ingredient of Sichuan cooking, it provides depth, heat, and a reddish colour. Sold in jars in Chinese supermarkets."
    },
    {
      "slug": "hui-guo-rou-technique",
      "term": "Twice Cooking",
      "definition": "A Chinese method of cooking meat twice: first boiled to tenderise and partially render fat, then stir-fried at high heat to colour and crisp the exterior."
    },
    {
      "slug": "leek-garlic-sprout",
      "term": "Garlic Sprouts",
      "definition": "Young garlic plants with mild, garlicky-sweet flavour. Traditional in twice-cooked pork. Leek tops or spring onion whites are the closest substitutes."
    }
  ],
