  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The name describes the method exactly. The pork is boiled until cooked through, chilled, then returned to a hot wok for a second round of cooking. This "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "hui-guo-rou-technique"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "twice cooking"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " fully renders the fat and gives the slices a slightly curled, crisp edge that cannot be achieved any other way."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The sauce is built on "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "doubanjiang"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "doubanjiang "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ". Traditional versions use "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "leek-garlic-sprout"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "garlic sprouts "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ". Leeks make an excellent substitute: use the green tops, cut into diagonal slices."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
